{"created": "2024-10-02T16:00:45.812159+00:00", "modified": "2024-10-02T16:00:49.440928+00:00", "id": 13882307, "conceptrecid": "3332807", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.13882307", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.3332807", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.13882307", "metadata": {"title": "Illustrations from The Turing Way: Shared under CC-BY 4.0 for reuse", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.13882307", "publication_date": "2024-10-02", "description": "<p>Illustrations created by <a href=\"http://www.scriberia.co.uk/\">Scriberia</a>&nbsp;as part of the&nbsp;<em>Turing Way</em> book dashes and illustration sprints in 2019 (two events in person), 2020 (one event in-person and one online), 2021 (two online), 2022 (Turing-Crick partnership project hybrid sprint, two Book Dash online), 2023 (latest Hybrid Book Dash in May 2023), 2024 May/June. They depict a variety of content of the five guides in The Turing Way as well as data science and the community activities of&nbsp;<em>The Turing Way</em>&nbsp;in general.&nbsp;More information on the book dashes can be found at <a href=\"https://the-turing-way.netlify.app/community-handbook/bookdash.html\">https://the-turing-way.netlify.app/community-handbook/bookdash.html</a>.</p>\n<p>When using any of the images, please include the following attribution with the specific DOI as listed on the particular Zenodo page:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><em>The Turing Way Community. This illustration is created by Scriberia with The Turing Way community, used under a CC-BY 4.0 licence. DOI: <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.3332807\">10.5281/zenodo.3332807</a></em></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>You can cite all versions by using the DOI&nbsp;<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.3332807\">10.5281/zenodo.3332807</a>. This DOI represents all versions, and will always resolve to the latest one.</p>\n<p>Please note that these images are shared here in the original format and size. We use smaller files in The Turing Way guides that you can find in our GitHub repository: <a href=\"https://github.com/alan-turing-institute/the-turing-way/tree/main/book/website/figures\">https://github.com/alan-turing-institute/the-turing-way/tree/main/book/website/figures</a>.</p>\n<p>Individual illustrations (in original size) are provided as <strong>.jpg</strong> files and zipped archives of the files (size &lt;1 MB for each image) are given in <strong>.jpg</strong> and <strong>.pdf</strong> (named starting with&nbsp;<strong>zz-&nbsp;</strong>to keep them at the bottom of the list). All releases provide individual illustrations (outside the compressed files) in their original size - you can browse them using the link provided on this page.</p>\n<p>The most recent release has been made from the May 2023 Book Dash event with the following zipped archives:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>zz-Latest-TheTuringWay-Scriberia-2024-May-allJPG-English-text.zip &lt;-- Latest JPG release</li>\n<li>zz-Latest-TheTuringWay-Scriberia-2024-May-allJPG-without-text.zip &lt;-- Latest JPG release without any text (for reuse purposes)</li>\n<li>zz-Latest-TheTuringWay-Scriberia-2024-May-allPDF-English-text.zip &lt;-- Latest PDF release</li>\n<li>zz-Latest-TheTuringWay-Scriberia-2024-May-allPDF-without-text.zip &lt;-- Latest PDF release without any text (for reuse purposes)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Images from the previous Book Dash from May 2019 - November 2022 are shared in the following zipped archives:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>zz-TheTuringWay-previous-Scriberia-2024-May-AllJPG-English-text.zip</li>\n<li>zz-TheTuringWay-previous-Scriberia-2024-May-AllPDF-English-text.zip</li>\n<li>zz-TheTuringWay-previous-Scriberia-2024-May-allJPGs-without-text.zip</li>\n<li>zz-TheTuringWay-previous-Scriberia-2024-May-allPDFs-without-text.zip</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Illustrations from the first two Book Dash have also released SVG files:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>zz-TheTuringWay-Scriberia-2019-20-SVG-where-available.zip.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Translating&nbsp;and editing for reusing Images:&nbsp;</strong>Zipped archives' names ending with '<strong>-without-text.zip</strong>' are provided for the latest release that can be translated into languages that you would like to use them in.&nbsp;We encourage the use and re-use of these images as much as possible. This includes remixing the images, for example changing the colours, translating text&nbsp;or merging them together with additional (openly licensed) images. If you create something that others may benefit from, we encourage you to contribute your image back to <em>The Turing Way. </em>Please contact the&nbsp;team members by emailing turingway@turing.ac.uk who can help you update this repository with the images you create.</p>\n<p>If you'd like to change the colours of the image to align with other elements of your presentation, <em>Turing Way</em> community member Alex Chan has written a <a href=\"https://alexwlchan.net/2020/02/adjusting-the-dominant-colour-of-an-image/\">guide for changing the dominant colour in an image</a> which we hope is helpful.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "The Turing Way Community", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Scriberia", "affiliation": null}], "resource_type": {"title": "Figure", "type": "image", "subtype": "figure"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "communities": [{"id": "the-turing-way"}], "relations": {"version": [{"index": 12, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "3332807"}}]}, "notes": "This work was supported by The UKRI Strategic Priorities Fund under the EPSRC Grant EP/T001569/1, particularly the \"Tools, Practices and Systems\" theme within that grant, and by The Alan Turing Institute under the EPSRC grant EP/N510129/1."}, "title": "Illustrations from The Turing Way: Shared under CC-BY 4.0 for reuse", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/13882307", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/13882307", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/13882307?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.13882307", "self_doi": "https://doi.or